{
  "description": "The conformance table of the wire validator every runtime carries: one family's wire description, one imported family's, and cases of a type expression, a JSON value, and whether the value is valid. The imported family's envelope carries the trace context and the meta every injected envelope carries, so that a slot of it is held to accepting traceparent, tracestate and a flat map of strings, and to refusing any of them at another type. The reserved nightseam. prefix of a meta key is the peer's rule and no facet of the type, so a reserved key passes the slot here and the frame carrying it is refused by the peer; tables/frames.json holds that. Both runtimes read this file. An invalid case carries the message the runtimes print for it, pointer and text as one string: the pointer names the member that was wrong and the text states the fact, and both runtimes are held to it word for word, so that a consumer whose server is in one language and client in the other reads one spelling of one refusal. A case crossing into an imported family carries the one pointer the value was handed in at, not a root per family it crossed. A case may supply slots with type expressions or imported families; both runtimes validate those explicit bindings. The equivalence rows hold generic applications to bound declarations. Generated Go codecs may leave a family slot unbound during schema preflight because the instantiated Go type validates it at marshal or unmarshal time; explicit applications never take that path. The patterns rows are the dialect a `pattern` facet is written in: ECMAScript syntax without lookaround and without backreferences, Nightseam's own regular-expression language, so that one declaration means one thing in every runtime. They are invalid at check time — the generator refuses a family that writes one, in both directions, the spellings only an RE2 engine reads and the ones only an ECMAScript engine reads alike — and a runtime refuses the same at validate time, since a descriptor can be hand-written or come from a target that skipped check.",
  "wire": {"types": {
    "Base": {"kind": "record", "fields": [{"name": "text", "type": "string", "required": true}]},
    "Payload": {"kind": "record", "extends": ["Base"], "fields": [
      {"name": "count", "type": "integer", "required": true, "min": 0, "max": 100},
